oderate} :question/id #uuid "c6d72e08-4063-53be-bc7f-e4ca6f106c12" :question/math-academy-id "q-130642" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${A}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${A}^{2}=A,$ so $A$ is an idempotent matrix. \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${A}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & ={A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b51e8ff1-247b-5efd-a684-8fca6c064e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce2acb8a-f100-5a93-9ce3-3f78a93129a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329022} {:answer/id #uuid "49004166-d47a-5eaf-8127-fe82cf434c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329023} {:answer/id #uuid "d959607a-4d16-50c2-9005-c2d696ff7eec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329024} {:answer/id #uuid "f66f9ece-7b66-5026-9eb7-6e1b39331316" :answer/type {:db/id