olution "First, we compute ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${C}^{2}=C,$ so $C$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${C}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{3} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot C \\\\  & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & ={C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{C}^{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b51e8ff1-247b-5efd-a684-8fca6c064e1e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Power of an Idempotent Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85718515-480f-51ed-871c-e22890c5e6e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 27 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183138} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c70f31-301d-5eec-ad41-9b27fba32a6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183139} {:answer/id #uuid "5380696b-843e-5d90-9278-4659cd526c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183140} {:answer/id #uuid "613ca3b6-8843-505f-bbc0-db80dd0c4042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 18 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183141} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5f3459-97fc-5db6-bcbf-a5cf4009befe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 